  "statement": "Let $f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{1-x}$. Show that $f(f(f(x)))=x$ for all $x$ in the domain.",
  "solution": "Compute $f(f(x))=\\dfrac{1}{1-\\frac{1}{1-x}}=\\dfrac{1}{\\frac{-x}{1-x}}=\\dfrac{x-1}{x}$. Then $f(f(f(x)))=f\\!\\left(\\dfrac{x-1}{x}\\right)=\\dfrac{1}{1-\\frac{x-1}{x}}=\\dfrac{1}{\\frac{1}{x}}=x$.",
  "hints": [
    "Compute $f(f(x))$ first.",
    "Then apply $f$ once more."
  ],
